Subject: [PATCH] FindStoneFor: reject items that are not weapons

WHY THIS PATCH EXISTS
    Every shield-carrying bot spams the red client error "Must have a Axe
    equipped", roughly every ten seconds, forever, while out of combat.

    `PlayerbotAI::FindStoneFor` switches on `pProto->SubClass` and never looks
    at `pProto->Class`. The item subclass enums are per-class and they overlap:
    in the pinned core fork's `src/server/game/Entities/Item/ItemTemplate.h`,
    `ITEM_SUBCLASS_WEAPON_POLEARM = 6` (line 350) and
    `ITEM_SUBCLASS_ARMOR_SHIELD = 6` (line 396) are the same integer, as are
    `ITEM_SUBCLASS_WEAPON_MACE2 = 5` (line 349) and
    `ITEM_SUBCLASS_ARMOR_BUCKLER = 5` (line 395).

    So a shield in the off hand is read as a polearm, `ImbueWithStoneAction`
    is handed a sharpening stone for it, and the server rejects the cast with
    SPELL_FAILED_EQUIPPED_ITEM_CLASS. The failure never stops: the retry guard
    in ImbueAction.cpp is `GetEnchantmentId(TEMP_ENCHANTMENT_SLOT) == 0`, and
    the only thing that would set that enchantment is the cast that fails.

    Full root-cause analysis, with the packet path and the reason the client
    renders the error as "Axe":
    plans/2026-08-23-playerbots-must-have-axe-equipped.md

WHAT WOULD LET THIS PATCH BE DELETED
    mod-playerbots gaining any item-class check in `FindStoneFor`. When that
    lands and AC_MODULE_SHA is bumped past it, this patch will stop applying
    and fail the build on purpose - at which point delete this file.

    Upstream PR: not yet opened. Add the link here when it is.

APPLIES TO
    mod-playerbots @ 8d9f6aa6bc6d45f9ae0ee0675b9b1f8aa6937312
    src/Bot/PlayerbotAI.cpp:5554-5601 (FindStoneFor)

--- a/src/Bot/PlayerbotAI.cpp
+++ b/src/Bot/PlayerbotAI.cpp
@@ -5560,6 +5560,15 @@
     if (!item_template)
         return nullptr;
 
+    // Sharpening stones and weightstones are weapon enchants, but the
+    // subclass checks below cannot tell a weapon from a piece of armour on
+    // their own: the subclass enums overlap. ITEM_SUBCLASS_ARMOR_SHIELD and
+    // ITEM_SUBCLASS_WEAPON_POLEARM are both 6, and ITEM_SUBCLASS_ARMOR_BUCKLER
+    // and ITEM_SUBCLASS_WEAPON_MACE2 are both 5, so without this guard an
+    // off-hand shield reads as a polearm and is handed a sharpening stone.
+    if (item_template->Class != ITEM_CLASS_WEAPON)
+        return nullptr;
+
     static const std::vector<uint32_t> uPrioritizedSharpStoneIds = {
         ADAMANTITE_SHARPENING_STONE, FEL_SHARPENING_STONE,   ELEMENTAL_SHARPENING_STONE, DENSE_SHARPENING_STONE,
         SOLID_SHARPENING_STONE,      HEAVY_SHARPENING_STONE, COARSE_SHARPENING_STONE,    ROUGH_SHARPENING_STONE};
